#============================================================================
# core_logic_is_not_paraconsistent.ath
#
# A PROOF IN ATHENA THAT CORE LOGIC IS NOT PARACONSISTENT
# Version 6 -- the refutation-system version. Athena member of the
# triple certification, faithful line by line to the Coq script
# core_logic_is_not_paraconsistent.v (Version 6) and to its Lean 4
# twin (Solution.lean); same twelve theorems, same block structure
# (A-F), same proof ideas, same names (transliterated to ASCII:
# F_M for the minimal reading, F_C for the Core reading, L- for
# Lukasiewicz-).
#
# WHAT CHANGED FROM THE PREVIOUS ATHENA VERSION (781 l., 2 axioms):
#
#   1. ZERO AXIOMS FOR THE ARGUMENT. The two commitments of Core Logic
#      -- Tennant's Claim 1 (Claim1-Tennant-hyp) and the refutation
#      rule anti-DNS.1 read as correct for F_C
#      (anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp) -- are no longer asserted: they are
#      HYPOTHESES, i.e. antecedents of the final theorems claim1-false
#      and claim1-false-at-zero-one. Every assert below is purely
#      definitional: datatype axioms (free generation) and the
#      defining biconditionals of mem, well-formed, derivable,
#      refut-wf, refutable -- the exact Athena counterparts of Coq's
#      Inductive declarations.
#
#   2. NO EXCHANGE RULE. The calculus locates the principal formula of
#      the left rules extensionally, by membership (mem), exactly as
#      [In _ Gamma] does in the Coq source. The old exch-rule
#      constructor is gone; contexts are pools of available
#      assumptions, and the only structural fact used is
#      context-monotonicity -- NOT Weakening (no new derivation is
#      created), NOT Cut: one and the same derivation tree, rebuilt
#      unchanged in a larger pool.
#
#   3. ATOMS ARE PEANO NATURALS (datatype Atom := zero | succ), as in
#      the Coq source (Var : nat -> formula). Reason: the closed
#      instance claim1-false-at-zero-one needs two PROVABLY distinct
#      atoms, and in Athena two meta-identifiers 'a, 'b are not
#      provably distinct without an extra axiom -- which would ruin
#      point 1. (zero =/= succ zero) is a free-generation axiom of
#      the datatype: the Athena counterpart of Coq's discriminate.
#
#   4. THE REFUTATION SYSTEM IS REIFIED, like derivations: datatype
#      Refut (constructors claim1-axiom and anti-DNS1) + refut-wf +
#      refutable -- a deductive system for NON-provability in the
#      sense of Lukasiewicz, Tiomkin (1988) and Goranko (Studia
#      Logica 53, 1994), with Claim 1 as its only rejection axiom and
#      anti-DNS.1 as its only refutation rule.
#
# THE TWELVE THEOREMS (Coq name -> Athena name):
#
#   DNS1_in_F                                DNS1-in-F
#   DNS2_instantiated                        DNS2-instantiated
#   DNS1_invertible_at_decisive_instance_in_F_M
#                            DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M
#   claim1_holds_in_F_M                      claim1-holds-in-F-M
#   DNS1_conclusion_underivable_in_F_M
#                                    DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M
#   anti_DNS1_holds_in_F_M                   anti-DNS1-holds-in-F-M
#   refutation_system_L_correct_for_F_M
#                                   refutation-system-L-correct-for-F-M
#   refutation_system_L_incorrect_for_F_C
#                                 refutation-system-L-incorrect-for-F-C
#   claim1_false                             claim1-false
#   claim1_false_at_0_1                      claim1-false-at-zero-one
#   claim1_holds_in_F_C                      claim1-holds-in-F-C
#   anti_DNS1_L_incorrect_for_F_C            anti-DNS1-L-incorrect-for-F-C
#
# plus the same auxiliary lemmas as in Coq: absurdity-core,
# context-monotonicity, DNS1-inversion-lemma (von Plato's method),
# refut-inversion, L-correct-aux.
#
# THE ARGUMENT IN ONE PARAGRAPH. DNS.1 is derivable in both readings
# (Block B) and invertible at the decisive instance in the minimal
# reading F_M (Blocks B-C): its premiss sequent A, not-A => B and its
# conclusion sequent (A->B)->B, not-A => B are BOTH underivable there.
# Hence the refutation system {Claim 1; anti-DNS.1} is L-correct for
# F_M (Block D). But that same refutation system is L-INCORRECT for
# the Core reading F_C (Block E): the decisive instance at the atoms
# 0, 1 is rejected by the system, yet derivable in F_C through
# R->C -- the derivation of DNS.2 from absurdity-core. Jointly,
# then, the two commitments of Core Logic refute themselves:
# claim1-false, closed at 0 and 1 in claim1-false-at-zero-one with no
# remaining hypothesis. Finally (Block F), Claim 1 is in fact TRUE of
# F_C (claim1-holds-in-F-C) -- and precisely for that reason
# anti-DNS.1 is L-incorrect for F_C (anti-DNS1-L-incorrect-for-F-C):
# Tennant cannot both keep Claim 1 and use the refutation rule his
# paraconsistency argument requires, the rule dormant in the shadow
# of the system.
#
# Generic methods (compression layer, in the style of the previous
# version): prove-trivia, wf-elim, mem!, mem2-cases!, sub-rewrite!,
# sub-cons!, un-derivable!, apply-mono!, neq-sym!, neq-atoms!,
# neq-formulas!, succ-neq!, none-neq!, into-disj3!, inv-ctx!,
# succ-impl-kill!, plus one introduction method per constructor
# (ax!, lneg!, rarrow!, larrow!, rac!, claim1-ax!, anti!, derivable!,
# refutable!). All constructions documented in FPMICS (Arkoudas &
# Musser): assert* with auto-quantification, chain with bidirectional
# equational justifications and [alternate], by-induction,
# datatype-cases, pick-witness, by-contradiction, from-complements,
# try, check, match with (some-list _)/(some-term _) patterns.
#
# Validated end to end (17 theorems, zero evaluation errors) against
# an Athena kernel built from the official sources
# (github.com/AthenaFoundation/Athena, SML/NJ image).
#============================================================================

# == Block A -- Language and calculus (Version 6 encoding) ==
#
# Reified derivations: datatype Deriv + well-formed + derivable.
# Faithful to core_logic_is_not_paraconsistent.v (Version 6):
# NO Exchange rule; the left rules locate their principal formula
# extensionally, by membership (mem), exactly as [In _ G] does in Coq.

# Atoms are Peano naturals, exactly as in the Coq source (Var : nat ->
# formula): the closed instance claim1-false-at-zero-one needs two
# PROVABLY distinct atoms, and (zero =/= succ zero) is a free-generation
# axiom of the datatype -- the Athena counterpart of Coq's discriminate.

datatype Atom := zero | (succ Atom)

datatype Formula :=
    (Var Atom)
  | (Neg Formula)
  | (Impl Formula Formula)

datatype Succedent :=
    none-succ
  | (some-succ Formula)

datatype Fragment := minimal-F | core-logic

datatype Deriv :=
    (ax-rule Fragment (List Formula) Formula)
  | (l-neg-rule Fragment (List Formula) Formula Deriv)
  | (r-arrow-rule Fragment (List Formula) Formula Formula Deriv)
  | (l-arrow-rule Fragment (List Formula) Formula Formula Succedent
                  Deriv Deriv)
  | (r-arrow-core-rule (List Formula) Formula Formula Deriv)

assert (datatype-axioms "Atom")
assert (datatype-axioms "Succedent")
assert (datatype-axioms "Formula")
assert (datatype-axioms "Fragment")
assert (datatype-axioms "List")

define formula-axioms := (datatype-axioms "Formula")
define neg-neq-impl  := (head formula-axioms)
define var-neq-neg   := (head (tail formula-axioms))
define var-neq-impl  := (head (tail (tail formula-axioms)))
define succ-axioms   := (datatype-axioms "Succedent")
define none-neq-some := (head succ-axioms)
define frag-axioms   := (datatype-axioms "Fragment")
define min-neq-core  := (head frag-axioms)

# --- Variable abbreviations ---

define [A B C]      := [?A:Formula ?B:Formula ?C:Formula]
define [G G']       := [?G:(List Formula) ?G':(List Formula)]
define [f f']       := [?f:Fragment ?f':Fragment]
define [S S']       := [?S:Succedent ?S':Succedent]
define [Sc Sc']     := [?Sc:Succedent ?Sc':Succedent]
define [d d1 d2]    := [?d:Deriv ?d1:Deriv ?d2:Deriv]
define [x y]        := [?x:Formula ?y:Formula]
define [a b]        := [?a:Atom ?b:Atom]
define atom-axioms  := (datatype-axioms "Atom")
define zero-neq-succ := (head atom-axioms)

# --- Membership predicate (the Athena counterpart of Coq's In) ---

declare mem : [Formula (List Formula)] -> Boolean

assert* mem-def :=
  [(~ (mem A nil))
   ((mem A (B :: G)) <==> (A = B | mem A G))]

# --- Well-formedness of a derivation tree ---
#
# The clauses mirror the five constructors of Coq's [derivable]:
# Ax, Lnot-, R->, L-> (by membership, no Exchange), R->C.

declare well-formed : [Deriv Fragment (List Formula) Succedent] -> Boolean

assert* wf-ax :=
  [((well-formed (ax-rule f G A) f' G' S)
      <==>
    (f = f' & G = G' & S = (some-succ A) & mem A G))]

assert* wf-l-neg :=
  [((well-formed (l-neg-rule f G A d) f' G' S)
      <==>
    (f = f' & G = G' & S = none-succ
     & (mem (Neg A) G)
     & (well-formed d f G (some-succ A))))]

assert* wf-r-arrow :=
  [((well-formed (r-arrow-rule f G A B d) f' G' S)
      <==>
    (f = f' & G = G' & S = (some-succ (Impl A B))
     & (well-formed d f (A :: G) (some-succ B))))]

assert* wf-l-arrow :=
  [((well-formed (l-arrow-rule f G A B Sc d1 d2) f' G' S')
      <==>
    (f = f' & G = G' & Sc = S'
     & (mem (Impl A B) G)
     & (well-formed d1 f G (some-succ A))
     & (well-formed d2 f (B :: G) Sc)))]

assert* wf-r-arrow-core :=
  [((well-formed (r-arrow-core-rule G A B d) f' G' S)
      <==>
    (f' = core-logic & G = G' & S = (some-succ (Impl A B))
     & (well-formed d core-logic (A :: G) none-succ)))]

# --- The predicate "derivable" ---

declare derivable : [Fragment (List Formula) Succedent] -> Boolean

assert* derivable-def :=
  [((derivable f G S) <==> (exists ?d:Deriv . (well-formed ?d f G S)))]

# == Generic toolbox (adapted to the Version 6 clauses) ==

# prove-trivia: proves a conjunction whose leaves are reflexive
# identities or sentences already in the assumption base.

define prove-trivia :=
  method (p)
    match p {
      (and (some-list conjuncts)) =>
        (!map-method prove-trivia conjuncts
           method (_) (!conj-intro p))
    | (= (some-term l) (some-term r)) =>
        check {(l equal? r) => (!reflex l) | else => (!claim p)}
    | _ => (!claim p)
    }

# wf-elim: elimination of a well-formedness clause; instance order to
# be validated empirically against the assert* quantifier order.

define wf-elim :=
  method (w clause instances)
    (!mp (!left-iff (!uspec* (head clause) instances)) w)

# The five introduction methods, one per constructor of Deriv.

define ax! :=
  method (fr Gamma phi)
    let { rhs := (fr = fr & Gamma = Gamma
                  & (some-succ phi) = (some-succ phi)
                  & (mem phi Gamma));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(well-formed (ax-rule fr Gamma phi) fr Gamma (some-succ phi))
          <== rhs                                            [wf-ax]])

define lneg! :=
  method (fr Gamma phi dprem)
    let { rhs := (fr = fr & Gamma = Gamma & none-succ = none-succ
                  & (mem (Neg phi) Gamma)
                  & (well-formed dprem fr Gamma (some-succ phi)));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(well-formed (l-neg-rule fr Gamma phi dprem)
                      fr Gamma none-succ)
          <== rhs                                            [wf-l-neg]])

define rarrow! :=
  method (fr Gamma phi psi dprem)
    let { rhs := (fr = fr & Gamma = Gamma
                  & (some-succ (Impl phi psi)) = (some-succ (Impl phi psi))
                  & (well-formed dprem fr (phi :: Gamma) (some-succ psi)));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(well-formed (r-arrow-rule fr Gamma phi psi dprem)
                      fr Gamma (some-succ (Impl phi psi)))
          <== rhs                                            [wf-r-arrow]])

define rac! :=
  method (Gamma phi psi dprem)
    let { rhs := (core-logic = core-logic & Gamma = Gamma
                  & (some-succ (Impl phi psi)) = (some-succ (Impl phi psi))
                  & (well-formed dprem core-logic (phi :: Gamma) none-succ));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(well-formed (r-arrow-core-rule Gamma phi psi dprem)
                      core-logic Gamma (some-succ (Impl phi psi)))
          <== rhs                                            [wf-r-arrow-core]])

define larrow! :=
  method (fr Gamma phi psi sc dleft dright)
    let { rhs := (fr = fr & Gamma = Gamma & sc = sc
                  & (mem (Impl phi psi) Gamma)
                  & (well-formed dleft fr Gamma (some-succ phi))
                  & (well-formed dright fr (psi :: Gamma) sc));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(well-formed (l-arrow-rule fr Gamma phi psi sc dleft dright)
                      fr Gamma sc)
          <== rhs                                            [wf-l-arrow]])

define derivable! :=
  method (fr Gamma S d)
    let { _ := (!egen (exists ?dd:Deriv . (well-formed ?dd fr Gamma S)) d) }
      (!chain<-
        [(derivable fr Gamma S)
          <== (exists ?dd:Deriv . (well-formed ?dd fr Gamma S))
                                                             [derivable-def]])

# == Block B -- Step 1: DNS.1 and DNS.2 are derivable ==

# Recursive membership prover: (!mem! phi L) concludes (mem phi L)
# whenever phi occurs syntactically in the list term L.

define mem! :=
  method (phi L)
    match L {
      (h :: t) =>
        check {
          (phi equal? h) =>
            (!chain-> [(phi = phi)
                       ==> (phi = h | mem phi t)   [alternate]
                       ==> (mem phi L)             [mem-def]])
        | else =>
            let { _ := (!mem! phi t) }
              (!chain-> [(mem phi t)
                         ==> (phi = h | mem phi t) [alternate]
                         ==> (mem phi L)           [mem-def]])
        }
    }

# sub-rewrite!: from (Gsmall = Gmid) and sub := (forall A . mem A Gmid
# ==> mem A Gbig), both in the base, concludes the subset sentence for
# Gsmall/Gbig.

define sub-rewrite! :=
  method (Gsmall Gmid Gbig sub)
    conclude (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gsmall) ==> (mem ?X Gbig))
      pick-any X:Formula
        assume (mem X Gsmall)
          (!chain-> [(mem X Gsmall)
                     ==> (mem X Gmid)  [(Gsmall = Gmid)]
                     ==> (mem X Gbig)  [sub]])

# sub-cons!: from sub := (forall A . mem A Gsmall ==> mem A Gbig) in
# the base, concludes the subset sentence for (phi::Gsmall)/(phi::Gbig).

define sub-cons! :=
  method (phi Gsmall Gbig sub)
    conclude (forall ?X:Formula .
               (mem ?X (phi :: Gsmall)) ==> (mem ?X (phi :: Gbig)))
      pick-any X:Formula
        assume h := (mem X (phi :: Gsmall))
          let { disj := (!chain-> [h ==> (X = phi | mem X Gsmall)
                                                             [mem-def]]) }
            (!cases disj
              (assume e1 := (X = phi)
                (!chain-> [e1 ==> (X = phi | mem X Gbig)     [alternate]
                              ==> (mem X (phi :: Gbig))      [mem-def]]))
              (assume e2 := (mem X Gsmall)
                (!chain-> [e2 ==> (mem X Gbig)               [sub]
                              ==> (X = phi | mem X Gbig)     [alternate]
                              ==> (mem X (phi :: Gbig))      [mem-def]])))

# un-derivable!: opens (derivable fr Gamma S) into its existential.

define un-derivable! :=
  method (fr Gamma S)
    (!chain-> [(derivable fr Gamma S)
               ==> (exists ?dd:Deriv . (well-formed ?dd fr Gamma S))
                                                        [derivable-def]])

# mem2-cases!: case analysis on a membership in a two-element context
# (h1 :: (h2 :: nil)): the methods m1, m2 handle the equality cases and
# must conclude goal; the nil case is discharged automatically.

define mem2-cases! :=
  method (hm x h1 h2 goal m1 m2)
    let { d1 := (!chain-> [hm ==> (x = h1 | mem x (h2 :: nil))
                                                         [mem-def]]) }
      (!cases d1
        (assume e1 := (x = h1) (!m1 e1))
        (assume e2 := (mem x (h2 :: nil))
          let { d2 := (!chain-> [e2 ==> (x = h2 | mem x nil)
                                                         [mem-def]]) }
            (!cases d2
              (assume e3 := (x = h2) (!m2 e3))
              (assume e4 := (mem x nil)
                (!from-complements goal e4
                                   (!uspec (head mem-def) x))))))

# apply-mono!: applies a monotonicity induction hypothesis ih (for the
# subtree dsub) to transport (well-formed dsub fr Gsmall S), known in
# the base, into (derivable fr Gbig S), using the subset sentence
# subsent (also in the base).

define apply-mono! :=
  method (ih dsub fr Gsmall S Gbig subsent)
    (!mp (!uspec (!mp (!uspec* ih [fr Gsmall S])
                      (!claim (well-formed dsub fr Gsmall S)))
                 Gbig)
         subsent)

#============================================================================
# THEOREM absurdity-core:  Var a, Neg (Var a) =>    in core-logic.
# Coq: L_neg (by membership) over Ax -- no Exchange in Version 6.
#============================================================================

define absurdity-core :=
  (forall ?a:Atom .
    (derivable core-logic
               ((Var ?a) :: ((Neg (Var ?a)) :: nil))
               none-succ))

conclude absurdity-core
  pick-any a:Atom
    let { va := (Var a); na := (Neg va); ctx := (va :: (na :: nil));
          t-ax   := (ax-rule core-logic ctx va);
          t-lneg := (l-neg-rule core-logic ctx va t-ax);
          _ := (!mem! va ctx);
          _ := (!mem! na ctx);
          _ := (!ax!   core-logic ctx va);
          _ := (!lneg! core-logic ctx va t-ax) }
      (!derivable! core-logic ctx none-succ t-lneg)

#============================================================================
# THEOREM context-monotonicity (Coq: Lemma context_monotonicity).
# NOT Weakening, NOT Cut: one derivation, rebuilt unchanged in a larger
# pool of available assumptions. Structural induction on Deriv.
#============================================================================

define context-monotonicity :=
  (forall ?d:Deriv .
    (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
      (well-formed ?d ?f ?G ?S) ==>
      (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
        (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
        (derivable ?f ?G' ?S))))

by-induction context-monotonicity {

  (ax-rule f0 G0 A0) =>
    pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (well-formed (ax-rule f0 G0 A0) fq Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-ax [A0 G0 Sq f0 Gq fq]) }
          pick-any Gp:(List Formula)
            assume hsub := (forall ?A:Formula .
                             (mem ?A Gq) ==> (mem ?A Gp))
              let { _ := (!chain-> [(mem A0 G0)
                                    ==> (mem A0 Gq)   [(G0 = Gq)]
                                    ==> (mem A0 Gp)   [hsub]]);
                    _ := (!ax! fq Gp A0);
                    _ := (!derivable! fq Gp (some-succ A0)
                                      (ax-rule fq Gp A0)) }
                (!chain-> [(derivable fq Gp (some-succ A0))
                           ==> (derivable fq Gp Sq)
                                            [(Sq = (some-succ A0))]])

| (dd as (l-neg-rule f0 G0 A0 d0)) =>
    let { ih := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                  (well-formed d0 ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                  (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
                    (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
                    (derivable ?f ?G' ?S))) }
    pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (well-formed dd fq Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-neg [A0 G0 Sq d0 f0 Gq fq]) }
          pick-any Gp:(List Formula)
            assume hsub := (forall ?A:Formula .
                             (mem ?A Gq) ==> (mem ?A Gp))
              let { sub0 := (!sub-rewrite! G0 Gq Gp hsub);
                    dprem := (!apply-mono! ih d0 f0 G0 (some-succ A0)
                                           Gp sub0);
                    ex := (!un-derivable! f0 Gp (some-succ A0)) }
                pick-witness dw for ex
                  let { _ := (!chain-> [(mem (Neg A0) G0)
                                        ==> (mem (Neg A0) Gq) [(G0 = Gq)]
                                        ==> (mem (Neg A0) Gp) [hsub]]);
                        _ := (!lneg! f0 Gp A0 dw);
                        _ := (!derivable! f0 Gp none-succ
                                          (l-neg-rule f0 Gp A0 dw)) }
                    (!chain-> [(derivable f0 Gp none-succ)
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp none-succ) [(f0 = fq)]
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp Sq)
                                                [(Sq = none-succ)]])

| (dd as (r-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 d0)) =>
    let { ih := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                  (well-formed d0 ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                  (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
                    (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
                    (derivable ?f ?G' ?S))) }
    pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (well-formed dd fq Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow [A0 B0 G0 Sq d0 f0 Gq fq]) }
          pick-any Gp:(List Formula)
            assume hsub := (forall ?A:Formula .
                             (mem ?A Gq) ==> (mem ?A Gp))
              let { sub0 := (!sub-rewrite! G0 Gq Gp hsub);
                    sub1 := (!sub-cons! A0 G0 Gp sub0);
                    dprem := (!apply-mono! ih d0 f0 (A0 :: G0)
                                           (some-succ B0) (A0 :: Gp) sub1);
                    ex := (!un-derivable! f0 (A0 :: Gp) (some-succ B0)) }
                pick-witness dw for ex
                  let { _ := (!rarrow! f0 Gp A0 B0 dw);
                        _ := (!derivable! f0 Gp (some-succ (Impl A0 B0))
                                          (r-arrow-rule f0 Gp A0 B0 dw)) }
                    (!chain-> [(derivable f0 Gp (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
                                                [(f0 = fq)]
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp Sq)
                                                [(Sq = (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))]])

| (dd as (l-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 Sc0 da db)) =>
    let { ihA := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                   (well-formed da ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                   (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
                     (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
                     (derivable ?f ?G' ?S)));
          ihB := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                   (well-formed db ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                   (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
                     (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
                     (derivable ?f ?G' ?S))) }
    pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (well-formed dd fq Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-arrow [A0 B0 G0 f0 Gq Sq Sc0 da db fq]) }
          pick-any Gp:(List Formula)
            assume hsub := (forall ?A:Formula .
                             (mem ?A Gq) ==> (mem ?A Gp))
              let { sub0 := (!sub-rewrite! G0 Gq Gp hsub);
                    subB := (!sub-cons! B0 G0 Gp sub0);
                    dl := (!apply-mono! ihA da f0 G0 (some-succ A0)
                                        Gp sub0);
                    exl := (!un-derivable! f0 Gp (some-succ A0)) }
                pick-witness dwl for exl
                  let { dr := (!apply-mono! ihB db f0 (B0 :: G0) Sc0
                                            (B0 :: Gp) subB);
                        exr := (!un-derivable! f0 (B0 :: Gp) Sc0) }
                    pick-witness dwr for exr
                      let { _ := (!chain->
                              [(mem (Impl A0 B0) G0)
                               ==> (mem (Impl A0 B0) Gq)  [(G0 = Gq)]
                               ==> (mem (Impl A0 B0) Gp)  [hsub]]);
                            _ := (!larrow! f0 Gp A0 B0 Sc0 dwl dwr);
                            _ := (!derivable! f0 Gp Sc0
                                    (l-arrow-rule f0 Gp A0 B0 Sc0 dwl dwr)) }
                        (!chain-> [(derivable f0 Gp Sc0)
                                   ==> (derivable fq Gp Sc0)  [(f0 = fq)]
                                   ==> (derivable fq Gp Sq)   [(Sc0 = Sq)]])

| (dd as (r-arrow-core-rule G0 A0 B0 d0)) =>
    let { ih := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                  (well-formed d0 ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                  (forall ?G':(List Formula) .
                    (forall ?A:Formula . (mem ?A ?G) ==> (mem ?A ?G')) ==>
                    (derivable ?f ?G' ?S))) }
    pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (well-formed dd fq Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow-core [A0 B0 G0 Sq d0 Gq fq]) }
          pick-any Gp:(List Formula)
            assume hsub := (forall ?A:Formula .
                             (mem ?A Gq) ==> (mem ?A Gp))
              let { sub0 := (!sub-rewrite! G0 Gq Gp hsub);
                    sub1 := (!sub-cons! A0 G0 Gp sub0);
                    dprem := (!apply-mono! ih d0 core-logic (A0 :: G0)
                                           none-succ (A0 :: Gp) sub1);
                    ex := (!un-derivable! core-logic (A0 :: Gp) none-succ) }
                pick-witness dw for ex
                  let { _ := (!rac! Gp A0 B0 dw);
                        _ := (!derivable! core-logic Gp
                                          (some-succ (Impl A0 B0))
                                          (r-arrow-core-rule Gp A0 B0 dw)) }
                    (!chain-> [(derivable core-logic Gp
                                          (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
                                                [(fq = core-logic)]
                               ==> (derivable fq Gp Sq)
                                                [(Sq = (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))]])
}

# --- Context abbreviations, shared by every statement below ---

define (claim1-ctx A) := (A :: ((Neg A) :: nil))
define (dns1-ctx A B) := ((Impl (Impl A B) B) :: ((Neg A) :: nil))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM DNS1-in-F (Coq: DNS1_in_F): DNS.1 is derivable uniformly in
# the fragment indicator f, hence at once in F_M and in F_C.
# Coq: L_arrow ( R_arrow (context_monotonicity H) | Ax ).
#============================================================================

define DNS1-in-F :=
  (forall ?f:Fragment ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    (derivable ?f (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==>
    (derivable ?f (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b)) (some-succ (Var ?b))))

conclude DNS1-in-F
  pick-any fr:Fragment a:Atom b:Atom
    let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
          iab := (Impl va vb); dns := (Impl iab vb);
          ctx1 := (claim1-ctx va); ctx2 := (dns1-ctx va vb) }
    assume H := (derivable fr ctx1 (some-succ vb))
      let { ex1 := (!un-derivable! fr ctx1 (some-succ vb)) }
        pick-witness d1 for ex1
          let { sub := conclude (forall ?X:Formula .
                                  (mem ?X ctx1) ==> (mem ?X (va :: ctx2)))
                  pick-any X:Formula
                    assume h := (mem X ctx1)
                      (!mem2-cases! h X va na (mem X (va :: ctx2))
                         (method (e1)
                           (!chain-> [e1 ==> (X = va | mem X ctx2)
                                                            [alternate]
                                         ==> (mem X (va :: ctx2))
                                                            [mem-def]]))
                         (method (e3)
                           let { _ := (!mem! na (va :: ctx2)) }
                             (!chain-> [(mem na (va :: ctx2))
                                        ==> (mem X (va :: ctx2)) [e3]])));
                ihd1 := (!uspec context-monotonicity d1);
                _ := (!apply-mono! ihd1 d1 fr ctx1 (some-succ vb)
                                   (va :: ctx2) sub);
                ex2 := (!un-derivable! fr (va :: ctx2) (some-succ vb)) }
            pick-witness d2 for ex2
              let { t-ra := (r-arrow-rule fr ctx2 va vb d2);
                    t-ax := (ax-rule fr (vb :: ctx2) vb);
                    _ := (!rarrow! fr ctx2 va vb d2);
                    _ := (!mem! vb (vb :: ctx2));
                    _ := (!ax! fr (vb :: ctx2) vb);
                    _ := (!mem! dns ctx2);
                    _ := (!larrow! fr ctx2 iab vb (some-succ vb)
                                   t-ra t-ax) }
                (!derivable! fr ctx2 (some-succ vb)
                             (l-arrow-rule fr ctx2 iab vb (some-succ vb)
                                           t-ra t-ax))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM DNS2-instantiated (Coq: DNS2_instantiated): DNS.2 in the
# Core reading, through R->C alone.
# Coq: L_arrow ( context_monotonicity (R_arrow_core HD) | Ax ).
#============================================================================

define DNS2-instantiated :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    (derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) none-succ)
    ==>
    (derivable core-logic (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
               (some-succ (Var ?b))))

conclude DNS2-instantiated
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
          iab := (Impl va vb); dns := (Impl iab vb);
          ctx1 := (claim1-ctx va); ctx2 := (dns1-ctx va vb) }
    assume HD := (derivable core-logic ctx1 none-succ)
      let { ex0 := (!un-derivable! core-logic ctx1 none-succ) }
        pick-witness d0 for ex0
          let { t-rac := (r-arrow-core-rule ((Neg va) :: nil) va vb d0);
                _ := (!rac! ((Neg va) :: nil) va vb d0);
                sub := conclude (forall ?X:Formula .
                                  (mem ?X ((Neg va) :: nil))
                                  ==> (mem ?X ctx2))
                  pick-any X:Formula
                    assume h := (mem X ((Neg va) :: nil))
                      let { disj := (!chain-> [h ==> (X = na | mem X nil)
                                                             [mem-def]]) }
                        (!cases disj
                          (assume e1 := (X = na)
                            let { _ := (!mem! na ctx2) }
                              (!chain-> [(mem na ctx2)
                                         ==> (mem X ctx2)    [e1]]))
                          (assume e2 := (mem X nil)
                            (!from-complements (mem X ctx2)
                               e2 (!uspec (head mem-def) X))));
                ih := (!uspec context-monotonicity t-rac);
                _ := (!apply-mono! ih t-rac core-logic ((Neg va) :: nil)
                                   (some-succ iab) ctx2 sub);
                ex1 := (!un-derivable! core-logic ctx2 (some-succ iab)) }
            pick-witness d1 for ex1
              let { t-ax := (ax-rule core-logic (vb :: ctx2) vb);
                    _ := (!mem! vb (vb :: ctx2));
                    _ := (!ax! core-logic (vb :: ctx2) vb);
                    _ := (!mem! dns ctx2);
                    _ := (!larrow! core-logic ctx2 iab vb (some-succ vb)
                                   d1 t-ax) }
                (!derivable! core-logic ctx2 (some-succ vb)
                             (l-arrow-rule core-logic ctx2 iab vb
                                           (some-succ vb) d1 t-ax))

# == Block C -- Step 2: DNS.1 is invertible in F_M ==

# Named injectivity axioms.

define var-inj  := (head (tail (tail (tail formula-axioms))))
define impl-inj := (head (tail (tail (tail (tail (tail formula-axioms))))))
define some-inj := (head (tail succ-axioms))

# neq-sym!: from the freshly derived (~ (l = r)), concludes (r =/= l).

define neq-sym! :=
  method (prem)
    match prem {
      (~ (= l r)) =>
        (!by-contradiction (r =/= l)
          (assume h := (r = l)
            (!absurd (!sym h) (!claim prem))))
    }

# neq-atoms!: concludes (x =/= y) provided (x =/= y) or (y =/= x) is in
# the assumption base.

define neq-atoms! :=
  method (x y)
    try {
      (!claim (x =/= y))
    | (!by-contradiction (x =/= y)
        (assume h := (x = y)
          (!absurd (!sym h) (!claim (y =/= x)))))
    }

# neq-formulas!: proves (p =/= q) for two structurally distinct formula
# terms, recursively, from the no-confusion and injectivity axioms; at
# the leaves, atom inequalities are looked up in the assumption base.

define neq-formulas! :=
  method (p q)
    match [p q] {
      [(Var x) (Var y)] =>
        (!by-contradiction (p =/= q)
          (assume h := (p = q)
            (!absurd (!chain-> [h ==> (x = y) [var-inj]])
                     (!neq-atoms! x y))))
    | [(Var x) (Neg y)]     => (!uspec* var-neq-neg [x y])
    | [(Neg y) (Var x)]     => (!neq-sym! (!uspec* var-neq-neg [x y]))
    | [(Var x) (Impl y z)]  => (!uspec* var-neq-impl [x y z])
    | [(Impl y z) (Var x)]  => (!neq-sym! (!uspec* var-neq-impl [x y z]))
    | [(Neg x) (Impl y z)]  => (!uspec* neg-neq-impl [x y z])
    | [(Impl y z) (Neg x)]  => (!neq-sym! (!uspec* neg-neq-impl [x y z]))
    | [(Impl p1 p2) (Impl q1 q2)] =>
        check {
          (p1 equal? q1) =>
            (!by-contradiction (p =/= q)
              (assume h := (p = q)
                (!absurd (!right-and (!chain-> [h ==> (p1 = q1 & p2 = q2)
                                                        [impl-inj]]))
                         (!neq-formulas! p2 q2))))
        | else =>
            (!by-contradiction (p =/= q)
              (assume h := (p = q)
                (!absurd (!left-and (!chain-> [h ==> (p1 = q1 & p2 = q2)
                                                       [impl-inj]]))
                         (!neq-formulas! p1 q1))))
        }
    }

# succ-neq!: given (Sq = (some-succ p)) in the base, and p, q
# structurally distinct, concludes (Sq =/= (some-succ q)).

define succ-neq! :=
  method (Sq p q)
    let { pq := (!neq-formulas! p q) }
      (!by-contradiction (Sq =/= (some-succ q))
        (assume h := (Sq = (some-succ q))
          let { e := (!chain [(some-succ p)
                              = Sq              [(Sq = (some-succ p))]
                              = (some-succ q)   [h]]) }
            (!absurd (!chain-> [e ==> (p = q) [some-inj]]) pq)))

# none-neq!: given (Sq = none-succ) in the base, concludes
# (Sq =/= (some-succ q)).

define none-neq! :=
  method (Sq q)
    (!by-contradiction (Sq =/= (some-succ q))
      (assume h := (Sq = (some-succ q))
        let { e := (!chain [none-succ
                            = Sq              [(Sq = none-succ)]
                            = (some-succ q)   [h]]) }
          (!absurd e (!uspec none-neq-some q))))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM DNS1-inversion-lemma (Coq: DNS1_inversion_lemma).
# Structural induction on derivations -- von Plato's method, adapted to
# extensional contexts: the induction is carried under an invariant on
# contexts included in {A, not-A, (A->B)->B}, and establishes that no
# F_M-derivation from such a context concludes B or A->B. The case
# r-arrow-core-rule is excluded by the fragment indicator: the Athena
# counterpart of Coq's (discriminate Hf).
#============================================================================

define (inv-succedents A B S) :=
  ((S =/= (some-succ B)) & (S =/= (some-succ (Impl A B))))

define DNS1-inversion-lemma :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (forall ?d:Deriv .
      (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
        (well-formed ?d ?f ?G ?S) ==>
        ?f = minimal-F ==>
        (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X ?G) ==>
          (?X = (Var ?a) | ?X = (Neg (Var ?a)) |
           ?X = (Impl (Impl (Var ?a) (Var ?b)) (Var ?b)))) ==>
        (inv-succedents (Var ?a) (Var ?b) ?S))))

conclude DNS1-inversion-lemma
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
            iab := (Impl va vb); dns := (Impl iab vb);
            body :=
              (forall ?d:Deriv .
                (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                  (well-formed ?d ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                  ?f = minimal-F ==>
                  (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X ?G) ==>
                    (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns)) ==>
                  (inv-succedents va vb ?S))) }
      by-induction body {

        (ax-rule f0 G0 A0) =>
          pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
            assume w := (well-formed (ax-rule f0 G0 A0) fq Gq Sq)
              let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-ax [A0 G0 Sq f0 Gq fq]) }
              assume hf := (fq = minimal-F)
                assume hinv := (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gq) ==>
                                 (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                  let { disj := (!chain->
                          [(mem A0 G0)
                           ==> (mem A0 Gq)                  [(G0 = Gq)]
                           ==> (A0 = va | A0 = na | A0 = dns) [hinv]]) }
                    (!cases disj
                      (assume e1 := (A0 = va)
                        let { _ := (!chain->
                                [(Sq = (some-succ A0))
                                 ==> (Sq = (some-succ va))  [e1]]) }
                          (!both (!succ-neq! Sq va vb)
                                 (!succ-neq! Sq va iab)))
                      (assume e2 := (A0 = na)
                        let { _ := (!chain->
                                [(Sq = (some-succ A0))
                                 ==> (Sq = (some-succ na))  [e2]]) }
                          (!both (!succ-neq! Sq na vb)
                                 (!succ-neq! Sq na iab)))
                      (assume e3 := (A0 = dns)
                        let { _ := (!chain->
                                [(Sq = (some-succ A0))
                                 ==> (Sq = (some-succ dns)) [e3]]) }
                          (!both (!succ-neq! Sq dns vb)
                                 (!succ-neq! Sq dns iab))))

      | (l-neg-rule f0 G0 A0 d0) =>
          pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
            assume w := (well-formed (l-neg-rule f0 G0 A0 d0) fq Gq Sq)
              let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-neg [A0 G0 Sq d0 f0 Gq fq]) }
              assume hf := (fq = minimal-F)
                assume hinv := (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gq) ==>
                                 (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                  (!both (!none-neq! Sq vb) (!none-neq! Sq iab))

      | (r-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 d0) =>
          let { ih := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                        (well-formed d0 ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                        ?f = minimal-F ==>
                        (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X ?G) ==>
                          (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns)) ==>
                        (inv-succedents va vb ?S)) }
          pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
            assume w := (well-formed (r-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 d0) fq Gq Sq)
              let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow [A0 B0 G0 Sq d0 f0 Gq fq]) }
              assume hf := (fq = minimal-F)
                assume hinv := (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gq) ==>
                                 (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                  let { left := (!succ-neq! Sq (Impl A0 B0) vb);
                        right :=
                          (!by-contradiction
                            (Sq =/= (some-succ iab))
                            (assume h := (Sq = (some-succ iab))
                              let { e := (!chain
                                      [(some-succ (Impl A0 B0))
                                       = Sq  [(Sq = (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))]
                                       = (some-succ iab) [h]]);
                                    c := (!chain->
                                      [e ==> ((Impl A0 B0) = iab) [some-inj]
                                         ==> (A0 = va & B0 = vb)  [impl-inj]]);
                                    pw := (!chain->
                                      [(well-formed d0 f0 (A0 :: G0)
                                                    (some-succ B0))
                                       ==> (well-formed d0 minimal-F
                                              (va :: Gq) (some-succ vb))
                                           [(f0 = fq) (fq = minimal-F)
                                            (G0 = Gq) (A0 = va) (B0 = vb)]]);
                                    hinv' := conclude
                                        (forall ?X:Formula .
                                          (mem ?X (va :: Gq)) ==>
                                          (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                                      pick-any X:Formula
                                        assume hm := (mem X (va :: Gq))
                                          let { d2 := (!chain->
                                                  [hm ==> (X = va | mem X Gq)
                                                             [mem-def]]) }
                                            (!cases d2
                                              (assume e1 := (X = va)
                                                (!chain->
                                                  [e1 ==> (X = va | X = na
                                                           | X = dns)
                                                             [alternate]]))
                                              (assume e2 := (mem X Gq)
                                                (!chain->
                                                  [e2 ==> (X = va | X = na
                                                           | X = dns)
                                                             [hinv]])));
                                    conj := (!mp (!mp (!mp
                                              (!uspec* ih
                                                [minimal-F (va :: Gq)
                                                 (some-succ vb)])
                                              pw)
                                              (!reflex minimal-F))
                                              hinv') }
                                (!absurd (!reflex (some-succ vb))
                                         (!left-and conj)))) }
                    (!both left right)

      | (l-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 Sc0 da db) =>
          let { ihA := (forall ?f:Fragment ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
                         (well-formed da ?f ?G ?S) ==>
                         ?f = minimal-F ==>
                         (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X ?G) ==>
                           (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns)) ==>
                         (inv-succedents va vb ?S)) }
          pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
            assume w := (well-formed (l-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 Sc0 da db)
                                     fq Gq Sq)
              let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-arrow
                                   [A0 B0 G0 f0 Gq Sq Sc0 da db fq]) }
              assume hf := (fq = minimal-F)
                assume hinv := (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gq) ==>
                                 (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                  let { disj := (!chain->
                          [(mem (Impl A0 B0) G0)
                           ==> (mem (Impl A0 B0) Gq)        [(G0 = Gq)]
                           ==> ((Impl A0 B0) = va | (Impl A0 B0) = na
                                | (Impl A0 B0) = dns)       [hinv]]);
                        goal := (inv-succedents va vb Sq) }
                    (!cases disj
                      (assume e1 := ((Impl A0 B0) = va)
                        let { _ := (!absurd e1
                                     (!neq-formulas! (Impl A0 B0) va)) }
                          (!from-false goal))
                      (assume e2 := ((Impl A0 B0) = na)
                        let { _ := (!absurd e2
                                     (!neq-formulas! (Impl A0 B0) na)) }
                          (!from-false goal))
                      (assume e3 := ((Impl A0 B0) = dns)
                        let { c := (!chain->
                                [e3 ==> (A0 = iab & B0 = vb) [impl-inj]]);
                              pw := (!chain->
                                [(well-formed da f0 G0 (some-succ A0))
                                 ==> (well-formed da minimal-F Gq
                                        (some-succ iab))
                                     [(f0 = fq) (fq = minimal-F)
                                      (G0 = Gq) (A0 = iab)]]);
                              conj := (!mp (!mp (!mp
                                        (!uspec* ihA
                                          [minimal-F Gq (some-succ iab)])
                                        pw)
                                        (!reflex minimal-F))
                                        hinv);
                              _ := (!absurd (!reflex (some-succ iab))
                                            (!right-and conj)) }
                          (!from-false goal)))

      | (r-arrow-core-rule G0 A0 B0 d0) =>
          pick-any fq:Fragment Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
            assume w := (well-formed (r-arrow-core-rule G0 A0 B0 d0)
                                     fq Gq Sq)
              let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow-core [A0 B0 G0 Sq d0 Gq fq]) }
              assume hf := (fq = minimal-F)
                assume hinv := (forall ?X:Formula . (mem ?X Gq) ==>
                                 (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
                  let { e := (!chain [minimal-F
                                      = fq          [hf]
                                      = core-logic  [(fq = core-logic)]]);
                        _ := (!absurd e min-neq-core) }
                    (!from-false (inv-succedents va vb Sq))
      }

# into-disj3!: sends an equality (X = h) into the three-way context
# disjunction, h being one of its members.

define into-disj3! :=
  method (e va na dns)
    match e {
      (= X h) =>
        check {
          (h equal? va) =>
            (!chain-> [e ==> (X = va | X = na | X = dns)  [alternate]])
        | else =>
            (!chain-> [e ==> (X = na | X = dns)           [alternate]
                          ==> (X = va | X = na | X = dns) [alternate]])
        }
    }

# inv-ctx!: proves the context invariant of the inversion lemma for a
# two-element context (h :: ((Neg va) :: nil)), h being va (context of
# Claim 1) or dns (context of the DNS.1 conclusion).

define inv-ctx! :=
  method (h va na dns)
    conclude (forall ?X:Formula .
               (mem ?X (h :: (na :: nil))) ==>
               (?X = va | ?X = na | ?X = dns))
      pick-any X:Formula
        assume hm := (mem X (h :: (na :: nil)))
          (!mem2-cases! hm X h na (X = va | X = na | X = dns)
             (method (e) (!into-disj3! e va na dns))
             (method (e) (!into-disj3! e va na dns)))

# --- Corollaries of the inversion lemma (Coq: Block C, Theorems 3-5;
#     ordering as in the Lean twin, where the invertibility is obtained
#     from the underivability of the conclusion) ---

#============================================================================
# THEOREM claim1-holds-in-F-M (Coq: claim1_holds_in_F_M): Claim 1 holds
# of F_M -- the premiss of the DNS.1 instance is underivable there,
# unconditionally, for distinct atoms.
#============================================================================

define claim1-holds-in-F-M :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (derivable minimal-F (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==> false)

conclude claim1-holds-in-F-M
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
            iab := (Impl va vb); dns := (Impl iab vb);
            ctx1 := (claim1-ctx va) }
      assume HD := (derivable minimal-F ctx1 (some-succ vb))
        let { ex := (!un-derivable! minimal-F ctx1 (some-succ vb)) }
          pick-witness d for ex
            let { hinv := (!inv-ctx! va va na dns);
                  conj := (!mp (!mp (!uspec*
                            (!uspec (!mp (!uspec* DNS1-inversion-lemma [a b])
                                         hab)
                                    d)
                            [minimal-F ctx1 (some-succ vb)])
                            (!claim (well-formed d minimal-F ctx1
                                                 (some-succ vb))))
                            (!reflex minimal-F));
                  conj2 := (!mp conj hinv) }
              (!absurd (!reflex (some-succ vb)) (!left-and conj2))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M
# (Coq: DNS1_conclusion_underivable_in_F_M): the conclusion of the
# DNS.1 instance is underivable in F_M as well.
#============================================================================

define DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (derivable minimal-F (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
               (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==> false)

conclude DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
            iab := (Impl va vb); dns := (Impl iab vb);
            ctx2 := (dns1-ctx va vb) }
      assume HD := (derivable minimal-F ctx2 (some-succ vb))
        let { ex := (!un-derivable! minimal-F ctx2 (some-succ vb)) }
          pick-witness d for ex
            let { hinv := (!inv-ctx! dns va na dns);
                  conj := (!mp (!mp (!mp (!uspec*
                            (!uspec (!mp (!uspec* DNS1-inversion-lemma [a b])
                                         hab)
                                    d)
                            [minimal-F ctx2 (some-succ vb)])
                            (!claim (well-formed d minimal-F ctx2
                                                 (some-succ vb))))
                            (!reflex minimal-F))
                            hinv) }
              (!absurd (!reflex (some-succ vb)) (!left-and conj))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M
# (Coq: DNS1_invertible_at_decisive_instance_in_F_M): the invertibility
# of DNS.1 at the decisive instance is a metatheorem of F_M. The
# antecedent is refuted by the underivability of the conclusion; the
# final step concludes from false -- the empty case analysis, not an
# ex falso axiom: the object calculus has no absurdity and no such rule.
#============================================================================

define DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (derivable minimal-F (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
               (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==>
    (derivable minimal-F (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b))))

conclude DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      assume HD := (derivable minimal-F (dns1-ctx (Var a) (Var b))
                              (some-succ (Var b)))
        let { _ := (!mp (!mp (!uspec* DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M
                                      [a b])
                             hab)
                        HD) }
          (!from-false (derivable minimal-F (claim1-ctx (Var a))
                                  (some-succ (Var b))))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM anti-DNS1-holds-in-F-M (Coq: anti_DNS1_holds_in_F_M):
# anti-DNS.1 holds in F_M as the CONTRAPOSITIVE of the certified
# invertibility -- Goranko's correctness discipline for refutation
# calculi: a refutation rule is licensed by the correctness of its
# converse.
#============================================================================

define anti-DNS1-holds-in-F-M :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    ((derivable minimal-F (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
     ==> false)
    ==>
    ((derivable minimal-F (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
                (some-succ (Var ?b)))
     ==> false))

conclude anti-DNS1-holds-in-F-M
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      assume hprem := ((derivable minimal-F (claim1-ctx (Var a))
                                  (some-succ (Var b))) ==> false)
        assume HD := (derivable minimal-F (dns1-ctx (Var a) (Var b))
                                (some-succ (Var b)))
          (!mp hprem
               (!mp (!mp (!uspec*
                       DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M [a b])
                       hab)
                    HD))

# == Block D -- Step 3: the refutation rule anti-DNS.1 and the
#    refutation system ==
#
# In the sense of Lukasiewicz, Tiomkin (1988) and Goranko (Studia
# Logica 53, 1994): a deductive system for NON-provability, made of
# rejection axioms and refutation rules. Below, the smallest refutation
# system that the kernel licenses: Claim 1 as its only rejection axiom,
# anti-DNS.1 as its only refutation rule -- the converse of the latter
# being the certified DNS1-invertible-at-decisive-instance-in-F-M.
# Refutation derivations are reified exactly as derivations are:
# datatype Refut + refut-wf + refutable.

datatype Refut :=
    (claim1-axiom Atom Atom)
  | (anti-DNS1 Atom Atom Refut)

assert (datatype-axioms "Refut")

define [rr rr'] := [?rr:Refut ?rr':Refut]

declare refut-wf : [Refut (List Formula) Succedent] -> Boolean

assert* rwf-claim1 :=
  [((refut-wf (claim1-axiom a b) G S)
      <==>
    (a =/= b
     & G = (claim1-ctx (Var a))
     & S = (some-succ (Var b))))]

assert* rwf-anti :=
  [((refut-wf (anti-DNS1 a b rr) G S)
      <==>
    (G = (dns1-ctx (Var a) (Var b))
     & S = (some-succ (Var b))
     & (refut-wf rr (claim1-ctx (Var a)) (some-succ (Var b)))))]

declare refutable : [(List Formula) Succedent] -> Boolean

assert* refutable-def :=
  [((refutable G S) <==> (exists ?rr:Refut . (refut-wf ?rr G S)))]

# List injectivity, needed to invert context equalities.

define list-axioms := (datatype-axioms "List")
define cons-inj    := (head (tail list-axioms))

# Introduction methods for the two refutation constructors.

define claim1-ax! :=
  method (x y)
    let { rhs := (x =/= y
                  & (claim1-ctx (Var x)) = (claim1-ctx (Var x))
                  & (some-succ (Var y)) = (some-succ (Var y)));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(refut-wf (claim1-axiom x y)
                   (claim1-ctx (Var x)) (some-succ (Var y)))
          <== rhs                                          [rwf-claim1]])

define anti! :=
  method (x y rprem)
    let { rhs := ((dns1-ctx (Var x) (Var y)) = (dns1-ctx (Var x) (Var y))
                  & (some-succ (Var y)) = (some-succ (Var y))
                  & (refut-wf rprem (claim1-ctx (Var x))
                              (some-succ (Var y))));
          _ := (!prove-trivia rhs) }
      (!chain<-
        [(refut-wf (anti-DNS1 x y rprem)
                   (dns1-ctx (Var x) (Var y)) (some-succ (Var y)))
          <== rhs                                          [rwf-anti]])

define refutable! :=
  method (Gamma S rtree)
    let { _ := (!egen (exists ?zz:Refut . (refut-wf ?zz Gamma S)) rtree) }
      (!chain<-
        [(refutable Gamma S)
          <== (exists ?zz:Refut . (refut-wf ?zz Gamma S))
                                                         [refutable-def]])

#============================================================================
# LEMMA refut-inversion (Coq: the inversion performed by [cases hprem]
# inside refutation_system_L_correct_for_F_M): any refutation of the
# Claim 1 sequent carries distinct atoms -- its last step can only be
# the rejection axiom, whose side condition is exactly a =/= b.
# Case analysis on the last refutation step; no induction is needed.
#============================================================================

define refut-inversion :=
  (forall ?rr:Refut .
    (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
      (refut-wf ?rr (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
      ==> ?a =/= ?b))

datatype-cases refut-inversion {

  (claim1-axiom a0 b0) =>
    pick-any x:Atom y:Atom
      assume w := (refut-wf (claim1-axiom a0 b0)
                            (claim1-ctx (Var x)) (some-succ (Var y)))
        let { _ := (!mp (!left-iff (!uspec* (head rwf-claim1)
                          [(claim1-ctx (Var x))
                           (some-succ (Var y)) a0 b0]))
                        w);
              xa := (!chain->
                      [((claim1-ctx (Var x)) = (claim1-ctx (Var a0)))
                       ==> ((Var x) = (Var a0)
                            & ((Neg (Var x)) :: nil)
                              = ((Neg (Var a0)) :: nil))   [cons-inj]
                       ==> (x = a0)                        [left-and var-inj]]);
              yb := (!chain->
                      [((some-succ (Var y)) = (some-succ (Var b0)))
                       ==> ((Var y) = (Var b0))            [some-inj]
                       ==> (y = b0)                        [var-inj]]) }
          (!by-contradiction (x =/= y)
            (assume h := (x = y)
              (!absurd (!chain [a0 = x    [xa]
                                   = y    [h]
                                   = b0   [yb]])
                       (!claim (a0 =/= b0)))))

| (anti-DNS1 a0 b0 r0) =>
    pick-any x:Atom y:Atom
      assume w := (refut-wf (anti-DNS1 a0 b0 r0)
                            (claim1-ctx (Var x)) (some-succ (Var y)))
        let { _ := (!mp (!left-iff (!uspec* (head rwf-anti)
                          [(claim1-ctx (Var x))
                           (some-succ (Var y)) a0 b0 r0]))
                        w);
              e := (!chain->
                     [((claim1-ctx (Var x))
                        = (dns1-ctx (Var a0) (Var b0)))
                      ==> ((Var x) = (Impl (Impl (Var a0) (Var b0))
                                           (Var b0))
                           & ((Neg (Var x)) :: nil)
                             = ((Neg (Var a0)) :: nil))    [cons-inj]]);
              _ := (!absurd (!left-and e)
                            (!neq-formulas!
                              (Var x)
                              (Impl (Impl (Var a0) (Var b0)) (Var b0)))) }
          (!from-false (x =/= y))
}

#============================================================================
# THEOREM refutation-system-L-correct-for-F-M
# (Coq: refutation_system_L_correct_for_F_M): everything the refutation
# system rejects is underivable in the minimal reading. Induction on
# the refutation derivation; both cases discharge through the
# inversion lemma.
#============================================================================

# Auxiliary form, quantified over reified refutation derivations --
# the Athena counterpart of Coq's [induction HR].

define L-correct-aux :=
  (forall ?rr:Refut .
    (forall ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
      (refut-wf ?rr ?G ?S) ==>
      (derivable minimal-F ?G ?S) ==> false))

by-induction L-correct-aux {

  (claim1-axiom a0 b0) =>
    pick-any Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (refut-wf (claim1-axiom a0 b0) Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!mp (!left-iff (!uspec* (head rwf-claim1)
                          [Gq Sq a0 b0]))
                        w) }
        assume hD := (derivable minimal-F Gq Sq)
          (!mp (!mp (!uspec* claim1-holds-in-F-M [a0 b0])
                    (!claim (a0 =/= b0)))
               (!chain->
                 [hD ==> (derivable minimal-F
                                    (claim1-ctx (Var a0))
                                    (some-succ (Var b0)))
                     [(Gq = (claim1-ctx (Var a0)))
                      (Sq = (some-succ (Var b0)))]]))

| (anti-DNS1 a0 b0 r0) =>
    pick-any Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
      assume w := (refut-wf (anti-DNS1 a0 b0 r0) Gq Sq)
        let { _ := (!mp (!left-iff (!uspec* (head rwf-anti)
                          [Gq Sq a0 b0 r0]))
                        w);
              hab := (!mp (!uspec* refut-inversion [r0 a0 b0])
                          (!claim (refut-wf r0
                                    (claim1-ctx (Var a0))
                                    (some-succ (Var b0))))) }
        assume hD := (derivable minimal-F Gq Sq)
          (!mp (!mp (!uspec* DNS1-conclusion-underivable-in-F-M [a0 b0])
                    hab)
               (!chain->
                 [hD ==> (derivable minimal-F
                                    (dns1-ctx (Var a0) (Var b0))
                                    (some-succ (Var b0)))
                     [(Gq = (dns1-ctx (Var a0) (Var b0)))
                      (Sq = (some-succ (Var b0)))]]))
}

define refutation-system-L-correct-for-F-M :=
  (forall ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
    (refutable ?G ?S) ==>
    (derivable minimal-F ?G ?S) ==> false)

conclude refutation-system-L-correct-for-F-M
  pick-any Gq:(List Formula) Sq:Succedent
    assume hR := (refutable Gq Sq)
      let { ex := (!chain->
              [hR ==> (exists ?rr:Refut . (refut-wf ?rr Gq Sq))
                                                       [refutable-def]]) }
        pick-witness r0 for ex
          assume hD := (derivable minimal-F Gq Sq)
            (!mp (!mp (!uspec* L-correct-aux [r0 Gq Sq])
                      (!claim (refut-wf r0 Gq Sq)))
                 hD)

# == Block E -- Step 4: the same refutation system is INCORRECT for the
#    Core reading -- and Claim 1 is false ==

#============================================================================
# THEOREM refutation-system-L-incorrect-for-F-C
# (Coq: refutation_system_L_incorrect_for_F_C): there is a sequent that
# the refutation system rejects and that F_C nevertheless derives --
# the decisive DNS.1 instance at the atoms 0 and 1.
#============================================================================

define one := (succ zero)

define refutation-system-L-incorrect-for-F-C :=
  (exists ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
    (refutable ?G ?S) & (derivable core-logic ?G ?S))

conclude refutation-system-L-incorrect-for-F-C
  let { h01 := (!uspec zero-neq-succ zero);
        ctx2 := (dns1-ctx (Var zero) (Var one));
        sb := (some-succ (Var one));
        _ := (!claim1-ax! zero one);
        _ := (!anti! zero one (claim1-axiom zero one));
        hrefut := (!refutable! ctx2 sb (anti-DNS1 zero one
                                        (claim1-axiom zero one)));
        hderiv := (!mp (!uspec* DNS2-instantiated [zero one])
                       (!uspec absurdity-core zero));
        _ := (!both hrefut hderiv);
        inner := (!egen (exists ?S:Succedent .
                          (refutable ctx2 ?S)
                          & (derivable core-logic ctx2 ?S))
                        sb) }
    (!egen (exists ?G:(List Formula) ?S:Succedent .
             (refutable ?G ?S) & (derivable core-logic ?G ?S))
           ctx2)

#============================================================================
# The two commitments of Core Logic, stated as HYPOTHESES -- nothing is
# asserted: they occur only as antecedents of the two theorems below.
#
#   Claim1-Tennant-hyp:      Tennant's Claim 1 for F_C -- the premiss
#                            sequent of the DNS.1 instance is
#                            underivable in Core Logic.
#   anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp: the refutation rule anti-DNS.1 read as
#                            correct for F_C -- the rule Tennant's
#                            paraconsistency argument needs, dormant in
#                            the shadow of the system.
#============================================================================

define Claim1-Tennant-hyp :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==> false)

define anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    ((derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
     ==> false)
    ==>
    ((derivable core-logic (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
                (some-succ (Var ?b)))
     ==> false))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM claim1-false (Coq: claim1_false): jointly, the two
# commitments refute themselves at every pair of distinct atoms.
# The derivation DNS2-instantiated (absurdity-core) witnesses the
# consequent that anti-DNS.1 forbids.
#============================================================================

define claim1-false :=
  (Claim1-Tennant-hyp ==>
    (anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp ==>
      (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom . ?a =/= ?b ==> false)))

conclude claim1-false
  assume h1 := Claim1-Tennant-hyp
    assume h2 := anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp
      pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
        assume hab := (a =/= b)
          (!mp (!mp (!mp (!uspec* h2 [a b]) hab)
                    (!mp (!uspec* h1 [a b]) hab))
               (!mp (!uspec* DNS2-instantiated [a b])
                    (!uspec absurdity-core a)))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM claim1-false-at-zero-one (Coq: claim1_false_at_0_1): the
# contradiction closed at the concrete atoms 0 and 1 -- no hypothesis
# remains other than the two commitments themselves.
#============================================================================

define claim1-false-at-zero-one :=
  (Claim1-Tennant-hyp ==> (anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp ==> false))

conclude claim1-false-at-zero-one
  assume h1 := Claim1-Tennant-hyp
    assume h2 := anti-DNS1-rule-for-C-hyp
      (!mp (!uspec* (!mp (!mp claim1-false h1) h2) [zero one])
           (!uspec zero-neq-succ zero))

# == Block F -- Step 5: Tennant is right about Claim 1 for F_C -- and
#    that is exactly why anti-DNS.1 is L-incorrect for F_C ==

# succ-impl-kill!: derives false from (sb = (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
# when sb = (some-succ vb) with vb atomic -- the common death of the
# r-arrow-rule and r-arrow-core-rule cases below.

define succ-impl-kill! :=
  method (sb vb A0 B0)
    (!absurd (!chain-> [(sb = (some-succ (Impl A0 B0)))
                        ==> (vb = (Impl A0 B0))          [some-inj]])
             (!neq-formulas! vb (Impl A0 B0)))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM claim1-holds-in-F-C (Coq: claim1_holds_in_F_C): Claim 1 is
# TRUE of Core Logic -- the premiss sequent A, not-A => B has no
# F_C-derivation. Case analysis on the last rule: no rule of F_C can
# conclude it. No induction is needed: every case dies on its
# side conditions.
#============================================================================

define claim1-holds-in-F-C :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    (derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var ?a)) (some-succ (Var ?b)))
    ==> false)

conclude claim1-holds-in-F-C
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      let { va := (Var a); vb := (Var b); na := (Neg va);
            ctx1 := (claim1-ctx va); sb := (some-succ vb);
            aux :=
              conclude (forall ?d:Deriv .
                         (well-formed ?d core-logic ctx1 sb) ==> false)
                datatype-cases
                  (forall ?d:Deriv .
                    (well-formed ?d core-logic ctx1 sb) ==> false) {

                  (ax-rule f0 G0 A0) =>
                    assume w := (well-formed (ax-rule f0 G0 A0)
                                             core-logic ctx1 sb)
                      let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-ax
                                    [A0 G0 sb f0 ctx1 core-logic]);
                            vbA := (!chain->
                              [(sb = (some-succ A0))
                               ==> (vb = A0)               [some-inj]]);
                            memq := (!chain->
                              [(mem A0 G0)
                               ==> (mem A0 ctx1)           [(G0 = ctx1)]]) }
                        (!mem2-cases! memq A0 va na false
                           (method (e1)
                             let { e := (!chain [vb = A0 [vbA]
                                                    = va [e1]]);
                                   ba := (!chain-> [e ==> (b = a)
                                                          [var-inj]]) }
                               (!absurd (!sym ba) hab))
                           (method (e3)
                             let { e := (!chain [vb = A0 [vbA]
                                                    = na [e3]]) }
                               (!absurd e (!neq-formulas! vb na))))

                | (l-neg-rule f0 G0 A0 d0) =>
                    assume w := (well-formed (l-neg-rule f0 G0 A0 d0)
                                             core-logic ctx1 sb)
                      let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-neg
                                    [A0 G0 sb d0 f0 ctx1 core-logic]) }
                        (!absurd (!sym (!claim (sb = none-succ)))
                                 (!uspec none-neq-some vb))

                | (r-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 d0) =>
                    assume w := (well-formed (r-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 d0)
                                             core-logic ctx1 sb)
                      let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow
                                    [A0 B0 G0 sb d0 f0 ctx1 core-logic]) }
                        (!succ-impl-kill! sb vb A0 B0)

                | (l-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 Sc0 da db) =>
                    assume w := (well-formed
                                  (l-arrow-rule f0 G0 A0 B0 Sc0 da db)
                                  core-logic ctx1 sb)
                      let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-l-arrow
                                    [A0 B0 G0 f0 ctx1 sb Sc0 da db
                                     core-logic]);
                            memq := (!chain->
                              [(mem (Impl A0 B0) G0)
                               ==> (mem (Impl A0 B0) ctx1)
                                                        [(G0 = ctx1)]]) }
                        (!mem2-cases! memq (Impl A0 B0) va na false
                           (method (e1)
                             (!absurd e1
                               (!neq-formulas! (Impl A0 B0) va)))
                           (method (e3)
                             (!absurd e3
                               (!neq-formulas! (Impl A0 B0) na))))

                | (r-arrow-core-rule G0 A0 B0 d0) =>
                    assume w := (well-formed (r-arrow-core-rule G0 A0 B0 d0)
                                             core-logic ctx1 sb)
                      let { _ := (!wf-elim w wf-r-arrow-core
                                    [A0 B0 G0 sb d0 ctx1 core-logic]) }
                        (!succ-impl-kill! sb vb A0 B0)
                } }
      assume HD := (derivable core-logic ctx1 sb)
        let { ex := (!un-derivable! core-logic ctx1 sb) }
          pick-witness d0 for ex
            (!mp (!uspec aux d0)
                 (!claim (well-formed d0 core-logic ctx1 sb)))

#============================================================================
# THEOREM anti-DNS1-L-incorrect-for-F-C
# (Coq: anti_DNS1_L_incorrect_for_F_C): precisely BECAUSE Claim 1 is
# true of F_C, the refutation rule anti-DNS.1 is L-incorrect for F_C:
# its premiss holds there while its conclusion fails there -- the
# derivation of DNS.2 is the counterexample. Tennant cannot both keep
# Claim 1 and use the rule his paraconsistency argument requires.
#============================================================================

define anti-DNS1-L-incorrect-for-F-C :=
  (forall ?a:Atom ?b:Atom .
    ?a =/= ?b ==>
    ~ (((derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var ?a))
                   (some-succ (Var ?b))) ==> false)
       ==>
       ((derivable core-logic (dns1-ctx (Var ?a) (Var ?b))
                   (some-succ (Var ?b))) ==> false)))

conclude anti-DNS1-L-incorrect-for-F-C
  pick-any a:Atom b:Atom
    assume hab := (a =/= b)
      (!by-contradiction
        (~ (((derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var a))
                        (some-succ (Var b))) ==> false)
            ==>
            ((derivable core-logic (dns1-ctx (Var a) (Var b))
                        (some-succ (Var b))) ==> false)))
        (assume H := (((derivable core-logic (claim1-ctx (Var a))
                                  (some-succ (Var b))) ==> false)
                      ==>
                      ((derivable core-logic (dns1-ctx (Var a) (Var b))
                                  (some-succ (Var b))) ==> false))
          (!mp (!mp H (!mp (!uspec* claim1-holds-in-F-C [a b]) hab))
               (!mp (!uspec* DNS2-instantiated [a b])
                    (!uspec absurdity-core a)))))
